{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ArchimedeanFunctorUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ArchimedeanFunctorUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousOn","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instBlochSuslinUniquenessZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instBlochSuslinUniquenessZero","kind":"instance","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L289-L292","doc":"**The instance.**  `D = 0`, which is the Bloch–Wigner dilogarithm on the\nreal line (`D(x) = Im Li₂(x) + arg(1-x) log|x| = 0` for real `x`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.blochSuslinUniqueness_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.blochSuslinUniqueness_iff","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L268-L287","doc":"**`BlochSuslinUniqueness D` holds exactly when `D = 0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.archimedean_functor_hyps_force_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.archimedean_functor_hyps_force_zero","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L260-L266","doc":"**The hypotheses of `archimedean_functor_uniqueness` force `τ_arch = 0`**\noff `{0,1}`, whatever `D` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pentagonCoherent_antisymm_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pentagonCoherent_antisymm_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L222-L258","doc":"**Every antisymmetric `PentagonCoherent` function vanishes off `{0,1}`.**\nNo continuity is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pentagon_at_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pentagon_at_inv","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L179-L220","doc":"Real-slice pentagon at `y = x⁻¹`: `f (x²) = 2 f x - 2 f (-x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.figure8_calibration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.figure8_calibration","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L122-L146","doc":"**Corollary (figure-8 calibration).**\n\nOnce a scalar `c` realising `τ_arch = c · D` has been fixed by the\nclassical Faddeev-Kashaev limit (the role played by\n`QOU.QPochhammer.ArchimedeanLimit`), the figure-8 archimedean\nvolume is determined: `Vol(4_1) = c · 2 · D(e^{iπ/3})`. The\nclassical normalisation gives `c = 1`, hence\n`Vol(4_1) = 2 · D(e^{iπ/3}) = 2 · Cl_2(π/3)` (Thurston 1978).\n\nThis corollary is purely book-keeping: the existence of the scalar\nis the content of `archimedean_functor_uniqueness`, and the value\nof the scalar is fixed by the classical limit. We state it as a\npredicate parameterised by the realisation function so the\nmanuscript-level claim has a Lean-level handle.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.archimedean_functor_uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.archimedean_functor_uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L90-L120","doc":"**Uniqueness of the archimedean realization functor (conditional).**\n\nLet `D : ℝ → ℝ` be the (real shape-parameter restriction of the)\nBloch-Wigner dilogarithm, and let `τ_arch : ℝ → ℝ` be the candidate\narchimedean realization on QOU motivic inputs. Assume\n\n* `BlochSuslinUniqueness D` — the classical pentagon-uniqueness\n  theorem of Suslin 1991, axiomatised;\n* `τ_arch` is continuous, antisymmetric, and pentagon-coherent —\n  the structural content provided by the cosimplicial / Yekutieli\n  triple machinery and the archimedean-limit conjecture\n  `QOU.QPochhammer.ArchimedeanLimit`.\n\nThen `τ_arch` coincides with `D` up to a single overall real scalar.\n\nThis is a real Lean proof (no `sorry`) that closes the conditional\nstatement modulo the two named classes. The QOU-novel content is\nthe conjunction of the four hypotheses on `τ_arch`; the classical\ninput is `BlochSuslinUniqueness`.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:archimedean-functor-uniqueness","label":"prop:archimedean-functor-uniqueness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.uniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.uniqueness","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The classical Bloch-Suslin theorem: any continuous antisymmetric\npentagon-coherent real-valued function on `ℝ \\ {0,1}` is a\nconstant scalar multiple of `D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.d_antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.d_antisymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L79-L79","doc":"`D` is antisymmetric: `D(1/x) = -D(x)` (Rogers' L-function form\nrestricted to the real shape locus; the full antisymmetry\n`D(x̄) = -D(x)` on `ℂ \\ {0,1}` projects to this on the real\nslice). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.d_continuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.d_continuous","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L74-L74","doc":"`D` is continuous on the open set where it is defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.d_pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.d_pentagon","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L72-L72","doc":"`D` itself is pentagon-coherent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinUniqueness","kind":"class","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L57-L88","doc":"Bloch-Suslin pentagon-uniqueness (Suslin 1991), packaged as a\ntypeclass over a fixed reference function `D : ℝ → ℝ` (the\nBloch-Wigner dilogarithm restricted to the real shape-parameter\nlocus). The classical theorem: any continuous antisymmetric\npentagon-coherent real-valued function on `ℝ \\ {0,1}` is a\nconstant scalar multiple of `D`. The class fields encode the\nrelevant input data; closure of any concrete instance reduces to\nthe K-theoretic rigidity of the Suslin map\n`K_3^{ind}(ℂ) → ℝ`, not yet in Mathlib.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PentagonCoherent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PentagonCoherent","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/archimedean-functor-uniqueness.lean#L40-L55","doc":"A real-valued function `f : ℝ → ℝ` is **pentagon-coherent** if it\nsatisfies the five-term identity at every pair of arguments where\nthe pentagon ratios are defined. We use the standard Rogers form\n\n    f(x) - f(y) + f(y/x) - f((1 - y⁻¹)/(1 - x⁻¹)) + f((1-y)/(1-x)) = 0.\n\nIn the multiplicative-group setting the identity is the defining\nrelation of the Bloch group `B(ℂ)` (Suslin 1991, §1).\n","signatureChunk":0}]}